[2.66, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[96m [*] OPAL TUI SHOWCASE ── Slide 1/34: [Welcome to Opal] ── [Overview & Markdown]\u001b[0m                \u001b[0m\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[3;1H                                                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b[4;1H                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[36m█\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[5;1H  # [*] Welcome to Opal TUI Framework                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[6;1H                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[7;1H                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[8;1H  Next-Generation Terminal User Interface & CLI DSL for Crystal                              \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[9;1H                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[10;1H  Opal unifies the best terminal engineering paradigms into a cohesive framework:            \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[11;1H    • [TEA] The Elm Architecture (TEA) — Pure, predictable state transitions (Bubbletea styl \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[12;1H    • [UI]  Declarative Fluent Styling & Themes — Lipgloss-inspired styling, 24-bit TrueColo \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[13;1H    • [FX]  Flicker-Free Delta Rendering — Blessed-inspired double buffering for 60fps smoot \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[14;1H    • [CTL] Rich Interactive Components — Multi-field forms, live fuzzy search, file dialogs \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[15;1H    • [VIZ] Terminal Data Visualizations — Sparklines, bar charts, pie charts, line graphs,  \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[16;1H                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[17;1H  │ \"Build world-class command-line interfaces with zero external C dependencies.\"           \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[18;1H                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[19;1H  ### >> Presentation Navigation Controls                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[20;1H    • Press [Shift+→] to advance to the next slide.                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[21;1H    • Press [Shift+←] to navigate back to the previous slide.                                \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[22;1H    • Press [ESC] at any time to exit and return to your shell.                              \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[23;1H    • Press [PageUp] / [PageDown] or [↑/↓] to scroll this markdown viewer.                   \u001b[0m\u001b[90m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[0m\u001b[24;1H                                                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[97m [Shift+→] Next  [Shift+←] Prev  [ESC] Quit │ [PageUp/Down] Scroll Markdown Document\u001b[0m            \u001b[0m"]
